es 1, 2, 3, 13, 14, 15, microphones are visible in front of each of the four seated individuals. The “X” symbols are iconic branding for the judges’ buzzers on *Britain’s Got Talent*.\n\n**4) Audience reactions toward the judges:**\n\n- While the audience is not directly shown reacting *to* the judges in most frames, the structure of the show (as seen in wide shots like 8, 25, 26) implies that the judges are the focal point of evaluation. The audience’s attention is directed toward the stage and judges’ table.\n\n**5) Judges providing feedback or reactions to performances:**\n\n- **Frames 12, 18, 19, 21:** Simon Cowell is shown speaking into a microphone, giving feedback.\n- **Frames 1, 2, 3, 13, 14, 15:** All four judges are shown reacting — smiling, clapping, or looking engaged — during performances.\n- **Frame 22:** A female judge (Amanda Holden) is shown in a close-up, likely giving feedback or reacting.\n\n---\n\n**Count of Distinct Judges Visible Across All Frames:**\n\n- **Simon Cowell** — visible in Frames 1, 2, 3, 12, 13, 14, 15, 18, 19, 21.\n- **Amanda Holden** — visible in Frames 1, 2, 3, 13, 14, 15, 22.\n- **David Walliams** — visible in Frames 1, 2, 3, 13, 14, 15 (seated second from left).\n- **Alesha Dixon** — visible in Frames 1, 2, 3, 13, 14, 15 (seated third from left, in pink/red outfit).\n\n✅ **Total distinct judges: 4**\n\n---\n\n**Conclusion:**\n\nThe video clearly shows **four judges** seated at the panel throughout multiple frames. Simon Cowell is one of them, but he is not the only judge. The answer “1” is therefore **incorrect**.\n\n**Correct Answer: 4**"}, {'batch_start': 90, 'batch_end': 120, 'image_paths': ['/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/vZV2WCKMsKs/frames/frame_0684.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/vZV2WCKMsKs/frames/frame_0848.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/vZV2WCKMsKs/frames/frame_0849.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/vZV2WCKMsKs/frames/frame_0850.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_pro